.\" Manual page for rdp-sessionmgr(8).  mdoc format.
.Dd May 25, 2026
.Dt RDP-SESSIONMGR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rdp-sessionmgr
.Nd privileged session broker for the Remote Desktop Protocol server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl df
.Op Fl s Ar path
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl S Ar service
.Op Fl X Ar path
.Op Fl m Ar WxH
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the privileged half of
.Xr rdpd 8 .
It receives authenticated session requests from the daemon over a
local
.Ux
socket, runs PAM (or
.Xr bsd_auth 3
on
.Ox ) ,
allocates the per-user runtime directory, and forks the
.Xr rdp-session 8
helper as the target user.
.Pp
On
.Ox ,
where
.Xr mount 2
and
.Xr unmount 2
are restricted to the superuser and forbidden by
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Nm
forks an unpledged root mount-helper at startup, before pledging and
before dropping privileges.
The pledged broker delegates each per-session
.Pa ~/RemoteDrive
fusefs mount and unmount to the helper over a socketpair, using one
fixed-size request structure per operation, and receives the
.Pa /dev/fuse0
descriptor back via
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS .
The helper validates the mountpoint, creates it with
.Dv O_NOFOLLOW ,
and mounts it through an
.Xr fchdir 2 Ns -pinned
target so a symlink in the user's home directory cannot redirect the
root mount.
A failure to mount is never fatal: the session simply runs without a
redirected drive.
.Pp
Failed authentication is rate limited per source IP: after 5 failures
within 60 seconds, further attempts from that IP are rejected without
running PAM or
.Xr bsd_auth 3
until the window passes; a successful login clears the counter.
The client IP is supplied by the
.Xr rdpd 8
worker in the authentication request.
.Pp
When a client disconnects, the
.Xr rdpd 8
worker sends a
.Sy SUSPEND
request carrying the backend file descriptor via
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS .
.Nm
stores the descriptor in a suspend slot tagged with the session's
logon ID.  When a new worker presents a
.Sy RESUME
request with a matching logon ID, the stored descriptor is returned
so the session continues without restarting.
.Pp
If the worker process dies before issuing
.Sy SUSPEND ,
.Nm
automatically suspends the session using the retained copy of the
backend descriptor.
Dead descriptors are validated by
.Xr poll 2
at resume time and reaped by a periodic sweep.
Suspended sessions expire after 120 seconds.
.Pp
When NLA authentication succeeds, the worker registers a random
16-byte nonce with
.Nm
via the
.Sy NLA_STORE
command and writes it to a token file.
A subsequent worker reading the token file must present the matching
nonce with the
.Sy NLA_AUTH
command; requests with a missing or incorrect nonce are rejected.
Pending nonces expire after 120 seconds.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Enable debug logging.
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground and log to standard error instead of
.Xr syslog 3 .
.It Fl s Ar path
Listen socket path.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/rdpserver/sessmgr.sock .
.It Fl u Ar user
Drop privileges to this user after binding the socket.
Only safe when
.Sy SPAWN
is not used.
.It Fl S Ar service
PAM service name.
The default is
.Ql login .
.It Fl X Ar path
Path to the
.Xr rdp-session 8
binary.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/sbin/rdp-session .
.It Fl m Ar WxH
Maximum desktop size, passed to each
.Xr rdp-session 8
as the framebuffer it allocates for dynamic resize.
The desktop can grow up to this size when the client requests a resize.
The default is
.Ar 3840x2160 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rdpd 8 ,
.Xr rdp-session 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Renaud Allard Aq Mt renaud@allard.it
